Q6 -> You are given two matrices A & B of same size, you have to return another matrix which is the sum of A and B.
Note: Matrices are of same size means the number of rows and number of columns of both matrices are equal.

Problem Constraints
1 <= A.size(), B.size() <= 1000 1 <= A[i].size(), B[i].size() <= 1000 1 <= A[i][j], B[i][j] <= 1000

Input Format
The first argument is the 2D integer array A The second argument is the 2D integer array B

Output Format
You have to return a vector of vector of integers after doing required operations.

Example Input
Input 1:
A = [[1, 2, 3],   
     [4, 5, 6],   
     [7, 8, 9]]  

B = [[9, 8, 7],   
     [6, 5, 4],   
     [3, 2, 1]]
 
Input 2:
A = [[1, 2, 3],   
     [4, 1, 2],   
     [7, 8, 9]]  

B = [[9, 9, 7],   
     [1, 2, 4],   
     [4, 6, 3]]
 
Example Output
Output 1:
[[10, 10, 10],   
 [10, 10, 10],   
 [10, 10, 10]]
Output 2:
[[10, 11, 10],   
 [5,   3,  6],   
 [11, 14, 12]]